  "prompt": "Improve the chess game to fix this critical multiplayer bug: When receiveOpponentMove is called, the opponent's move must be applied to the CURRENT local board state, not replace it entirely. \n\nFix receiveOpponentMove to work like this:\n\nwindow.receiveOpponentMove = function(moveData) {\n  if (!moveData || !moveData.action) return;\n  \n  const from = moveData.action.from;\n  const to = moveData.action.to;\n  \n  // Apply move to current board\n  const piece = board[from.row][from.col];\n  if (!piece) return;\n  \n  // Handle capture\n  const captured = board[to.row][to.col];\n  if (captured) {\n    capturedPieces[captured.color] = capturedPieces[captured.color] || [];\n    capturedPieces[captured.color].push(captured);\n  }\n  \n  // Move piece\n  board[to.row][to.col] = piece;\n  board[from.row][from.col] = null;\n  \n  // Switch turn\n  currentTurn = currentTurn === 'white' ? 'black' : 'white';\n  \n  // Re-render\n  renderBoard();\n  updateTurnIndicator();\n  updateCapturedPieces();\n};\n\nDo NOT use gameState.board from moveData to replace the entire board. Only use action.from and action.to to apply the move. This ensures both players always have consistent board state.",
